WEBVTT

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:43.670
Reptiles and amphibians are sometimes thought of as primitive, dull and dim-witted.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:53.150
In fact, of course, they can be lethally fast, spectacularly beautiful, surprisingly affectionate and very sophisticated.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:07.250
They have remarkably varied ways of catching their prey and of defending themselves.

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:17.330
They can produce a great turn of speed and fight with impressive zest.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.840
Some have spectacular colours and show off to one another.

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:45.210
They communicate with calls and with gestures.

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:51.150
And there, that's it.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:54.730
The fool works.

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:59.290
Reptiles have scaly skin.

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:03.140
and amphibians, soft, moist ones.

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:09.210
None of them live at a uniform pace,

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:13.850
but switch from the fast to the slow lane within a year or an hour.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:21.900
Unlike us, they get their energy directly from the sun.

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:29.010
And although being called cold-blooded might suggest they are unemotional,

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:29.980
they can...

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:53.770
touchingly warm-hearted as mates and as parents. That's just the beginning. There are a whole lot

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:59.920
of other warm-hearted truths that give the phrase life in cold blood.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:19.260
completely new meaning. The Galapagos Islands. Some of the reptiles that live here are particularly

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:26.670
skilful at solving the problems of getting their energy directly from sunshine. Marine

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:29.980
iguanas face a major thermal...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:38.040
challenge every morning of their lives. During the night their bodies cool and now they must warm up

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:45.940
quickly in order that they can become active and start feeding. Their bodies and skins are black

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:54.340
which is very efficient at absorbing heat and they bask with their black flanks broadside to the sun.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:04.760
The rate at which they absorb warmth is invisible to the naked eye,

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:08.240
but very clear indeed to a thermal camera.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:12.320
First thing, they're cold and purplish blue,

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:18.080
but slowly, as they warm up, a golden glow spreads through their bodies.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:24.540
And eventually, after half an hour or so, they become as hot as the rocks beneath them.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:29.980
Once they're thoroughly warmed up, marine iguanas can maintain their...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:36.690
body temperature just about as constantly as i can and what's more at about the same level or indeed

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:45.880
slightly higher around 37 degrees centigrade now they need to feed there's nothing to eat

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:53.990
on or around these barren rocks except seaweed and to get that they'll have to swim but the sea

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:59.360
around here is surprisingly cold, around 15 to 16 degrees.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:07.670
centigrade. And only the bigger iguanas can absorb enough heat to power the dives to enable

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:18.760
them to go to the seaweed at any depth. However, their bodies are now thoroughly warmed up. The

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:25.160
thermal camera shows them as golden yellow as they clamber down over the cold blue rocks

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:26.950
and dive into the sea.

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:47.630
Although their islands lie almost exactly on the equator,

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:51.950
the sea here is permanently chilled by a cold current

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:54.270
that sweeps up from the depths of the ocean.

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:57.810
So they won't be able to stay in the water for very long.

00:05:58.540 --> 00:05:59.920
They have no time to waste.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:06.340
In the shallows, close to the shore, the seaweed has been heavily cropped.

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:12.050
To get a good meal, they may have to dive to at least 15 feet, 5 metres.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:18.490
They're able to reduce the chilling effect of the cold water

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:23.070
by closing down the blood supply to their limbs and the outer part of their bodies.

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:28.070
But even so, their body temperature may drop by 10 degrees or so.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:29.980
A cooling like that...

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:32.000
would kill a human diver.

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:38.480
After five to ten minutes on the seafloor,

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:40.280
most iguanas have had enough

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:42.270
and they return to the surface

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:45.250
and the life-saving warmth of the rocky shore.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:53.770
A recently emerged iguana is black.

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:55.510
It's chilled to the bone.

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:06.830
Now they need heat in order to be able to digest that meal of seaweed.

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:13.640
And they get that by spread-eagling themselves on these black, hot, sun-baked rocks.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:26.060
Their image warms from black, purple, and then from red to orange.

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:35.920
In the evening, the temperature falls and they huddle together to retain their warmth as long as possible.

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:48.550
They will have to wait until the following morning before they can re-warm themselves sufficiently to feed again.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:54.980
Most kinds of lizards have this daily schedule.

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:58.450
Side-blotched lizards in California certainly do.

00:07:59.460 --> 00:07:59.980
You can see...

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:06.710
from the colour of my face that my body is warm. That's because I've got a central heating system

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:13.990
which I've fuelled with my breakfast. In fact, about 80% of what I eat is used in keeping my body

00:08:13.990 --> 00:08:20.200
temperature high and steady. These lizards, however, squander very little of the energy

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:25.680
they get from their food on warming themselves. They, like the marine iguanas, get nearly all

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:28.600
they need for that by basking on the warm rocks.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.400
And so important is the need for warmth

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:37.040
that the females actually choose their males

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:40.980
on the basis of which has the best underfloor heating.

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:47.820
Each male sits on his pile of boulders doing press-ups

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:51.060
to signal his ownership and to warn off other males.

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:56.900
Intruders are confronted immediately and, if necessary, attacked.

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:15.150
and the victor returns to sit on his wonderfully warm throne.

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:23.870
Look at his rocky kingdom with a thermal camera,

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:26.430
and it's immediately clear why it's so precious.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:29.980
The rocks are very much hotter than the surrounding grasslands.

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:35.120
and big tall ones catch the sun earlier and retain its heat longer.

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:40.830
So not only does the sun warm him from above, his rocks do from beneath.

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:46.860
The most powerful dominant male has, naturally, the best pile of rocks,

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:51.340
and not surprisingly, almost all the females.

00:09:57.720 --> 00:09:59.980
But is it the males themselves, or the...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:06.920
their assets that the females are interested in. To find out, let's move their hot rocks

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:27.620
and give them to a subordinate male. Females quickly recognize that a more desirable residence

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:29.960
has appeared in the neighborhood and...

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:40.690
start to move across, and the sex-starved wimp suddenly finds himself amazingly popular.

00:10:44.270 --> 00:10:49.660
So, the females do indeed go for the males with the hottest rocks.

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:58.280
These lizards, on a small islet off the shores of Menorca in the Mediterranean,

00:10:58.660 --> 00:10:59.960
get their heat from...

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:14.140
another and very unusual source. Ow! They're very curious. I'm the new boy on the block,

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:23.720
the new object in their environment, and that one just gave me a little nip. They investigate

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:28.360
the world around them by tasting it, and they're still trying to work out what I am.

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:37.210
Their island is rocky and not particularly rich in food.

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.960
The lizards are primarily insect eaters,

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:43.040
but during the flowering season they also take nectar.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:46.720
They collect it from plants, like spurge, which is very common.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:51.140
And they have a very special relationship with this flower.

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:54.710
It's called the dead horse, Arum.

00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:57.530
And it certainly looks like carrion and...

00:11:58.230 --> 00:11:59.670
Of course it does.

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:02.670
It smells very strongly of carrion.

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:08.080
As a consequence of both its looks and its smell, it attracts carrion flies.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:12.110
And of course, it's the flies that the lizards are after.

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:21.180
But as well as providing food for the lizards, this extraordinary flower helps them in another way.

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:29.830
If this central part, which is called the spadix, is slightly warm, as you can see.

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:31.030
from a thermal camera.

00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:36.120
The chemical process that produces the disgusting smell

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:40.060
also creates heat and raises the temperature of the flower

00:12:40.060 --> 00:12:42.640
by up to five degrees above the surroundings,

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:46.960
sufficiently high for a lizard to warm itself on it on a cold morning.

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:49.630
And in case you find that hard to believe,

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:52.560
here is confirmation from the thermal camera.

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:56.850
The purplish-blue lizard quickly takes on the same temperature

00:12:56.850 --> 00:12:58.690
and colour as the arum.

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:08.200
And sitting on Aran's brings another benefit.

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:16.980
A fly, lured by the smell, crawls inside.

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:23.490
The lizard hears the fly buzzing within.

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:29.970
The fly, of course, can't find anything it wants, but now it can't get out.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:33.420
The entrance to the flower is blocked by the lizard.

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:46.700
The lizard gets an easy meal.

00:13:55.720 --> 00:13:59.800
Two months later, the air and flowers have shriveled and produced their fruit.

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:07.260
